---
// Home (design: Main). The claim, the app, the family live, the registry in one line each.
import Popular from "../components/home/Popular.astro";
import Tour from "../components/home/Tour.astro";
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
---
<Page current="home" news="Postgres extensions by name" newsHref="/registry/extensions/">
<div class="mn mn-s1">

  <!-- Hero: the claim, the brand line, the install line as the call -->
  <section class="mn-s2">
    <h1 class="mn-hero-title mn-s3">Your laptop is a beast. Stop making it run a VM.</h1>
    <p class="mn-hero-tag mn-s4">Run your whole stack. Feel none of it.</p>
    <p class="mn-s5">Real Postgres, Kafka and a whole local AWS, running natively on your Mac. Awake the moment your code calls. Asleep the moment it stops.</p>
    <div class="mn-stack-sm mn-install mn-s6">
      <a class="mn-btn mn-btn-lamp" href="/download/">Download for Mac</a>
      <div class="mn-s7">
        <code class="mn-s8"><span class="mn-s9">$</span> brew install --cask doze-dev/tap/doze</code>
        <button class="mn-s10" type="button" data-copy="brew install --cask doze-dev/tap/doze" aria-label="Copy the install command">Copy</button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <span class="mn-s11">Free and open source · Apple silicon and Linux · no account, no telemetry · <a href="/download/">other ways to install</a></span>
  </section>

  <!-- The real app, staged -->
  <section class="mn-s12">
    <div class="mn-s13"></div>
    <div class="mn-win mn-s14">
      <div class="mn-bar"><span class="mn-dot mn-s15"></span><span class="mn-dot mn-s16"></span><span class="mn-dot mn-s17"></span><span class="mn-s18">doze</span></div>
      <img class="mn-s19" src="/media/app-map.webp" alt="The doze app's map of a demo stack: some services awake, some dozing, some asleep">
    </div>
    <div class="mn-float mn-s20">
      <div class="mn-s21">
        <img class="mn-s22" src="/media/app-stack.webp" alt="A database tile from the demo stack: awake, with its open connections">
      </div>
      <div class="mn-s23"><b class="mn-s24">asleep → awake</b> on the first connection</div>
    </div>
    <div class="mn-float mn-s25">
      <div class="mn-s26">Stacks</div>
      <div class="mn-s27"><span>●&#160;&#160;larder</span><span class="mn-s28">›</span></div>
      <div class="mn-s29"><span>○&#160;&#160;acme</span><span class="mn-s28">›</span></div>
      <div class="mn-s30"></div>
      <div class="mn-s31">Quit doze · stacks keep running</div>
    </div>
    <p class="mn-s32">The doze app, from its demo stack. Quit it and your stacks keep running. <span class="mn-recap">[re-capture with Larder]</span></p>
  </section>

  <!-- The family, live -->
  <section class="mn-s33">
    <div class="mn-s34">
      <span class="mn-eyebrow">Live, not mocked</span>
      <h2 class="mn-h2">Watch all three work.</h2>
    </div>
    <Tour set="family" />
  </section>

  <!-- Sound familiar? -->
  <section class="mn-s35" id="familiar">
    <div class="mn-s36">
      <span class="mn-eyebrow">Sound familiar?</span>
      <h2 class="mn-h2 mn-s37">Local development is a mess nobody signed up for.</h2>
      <p class="mn-s38">Containers, brew services, half-remembered ports and a setup doc that worked once. You didn't choose it. It just grew.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mn-s39">
      <div class="mn-pain"><span class="mn-old">fans: full tilt · battery: 31%</span><h3 class="mn-s40">Your laptop sounds like it's leaving.</h3><p class="mn-s41">A VM full of databases runs all day, used or not. doze runs nothing until something connects.</p></div>
      <div class="mn-pain"><span class="mn-old">breakpoint never hit</span><h3 class="mn-s40">Debugging through a wall.</h3><p class="mn-s41">No VM, no volume mounts, no forwarded debug ports. Real processes on your machine. Attach and go.</p></div>
      <div class="mn-pain"><span class="mn-old">port 5432 is already allocated</span><h3 class="mn-s40">Port roulette.</h3><p class="mn-s41">Every service gets a name and an address of its own. Two projects, both on 5432, no clash.</p></div>
      <div class="mn-pain"><span class="mn-old">localhost:3000? :3001? :8080?</span><h3 class="mn-s40">Which one was the gateway again?</h3><p class="mn-s41"><code class="mn-s42">gateway.larder.doze</code>. And https on your own domain when OAuth refuses localhost.</p></div>
      <div class="mn-pain"><span class="mn-old">README.md · last updated 2023</span><h3 class="mn-s40">Onboarding takes a day.</h3><p class="mn-s41">One doze.hcl in the repo. A new teammate clones it and runs <code class="mn-s42">doze up</code>.</p></div>
      <div class="mn-pain"><span class="mn-old">docker ps -a · 23 exited</span><h3 class="mn-s40">The graveyard of forgotten stacks.</h3><p class="mn-s41">The menu bar shows every stack and what's awake, and cleans up what was left behind.</p></div>
    </div>
    <a class="mn-s43" href="/tuesday/">Walk through a Tuesday →</a>
  </section>

  <!-- Instead of -->
  <section class="mn-s44">
    <div class="mn-s45">
      <h2 class="mn-h2">Three tools. Three things you can uninstall.</h2>
      <div class="mn-s46">
        <a class="mn-s47" href="/doze/">
          <div class="mn-s48"><img class="mn-s49" src="/media/app-stack.webp" alt="The doze app's tiles, from its demo stack"></div>
          <div class="mn-s50">
            <div class="mn-s51"><img class="mn-s52" src="/brand/doze.svg" alt=""><b class="mn-s53">doze</b></div>
            <span class="mn-s54">Instead of <s>Docker Desktop for your databases</s></span>
            <p class="mn-s55">Your whole stack, on demand.</p>
          </div>
        </a>
        <a class="mn-s47" href="/aws/">
          <div class="mn-s56"><img class="mn-s49" src="/media/aws-wire.webp" alt="The doze AWS console's wire: every call the app made"></div>
          <div class="mn-s50">
            <div class="mn-s51"><img class="mn-s52" src="/brand/doze-aws.svg" alt=""><b class="mn-s53">doze AWS</b></div>
            <span class="mn-s54">Instead of <s>an emulator in a container, or the shared dev account</s></span>
            <p class="mn-s57">All of AWS. None of the account.</p>
          </div>
        </a>
        <a class="mn-s47" href="/kafka/">
          <div class="mn-s58"><img class="mn-s49" src="/media/kafka-orders.webp" alt="The doze Kafka console: a topic and its messages"></div>
          <div class="mn-s50">
            <div class="mn-s51"><img class="mn-s52" src="/brand/doze-kafka.svg" alt=""><b class="mn-s53">doze Kafka</b></div>
            <span class="mn-s54">Instead of <s>a JVM, ZooKeeper and a quorum in containers</s></span>
            <p class="mn-s59">Kafka. Hold the JVM.</p>
          </div>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Larder: a real project, not a toy -->
  <section class="mn-s60">
    <div class="mn-s61">
      <span class="mn-eyebrow">Try it on Larder</span>
      <h2 class="mn-h2">A real project, not a toy.</h2>
      <p class="mn-s62">Larder is a made-up online grocer: groceries at your door within the hour. It is built the way real backends end up: a monorepo split by domain, each team in the language it knows, held together by Kafka topics and HTTP. Nine services, three languages, five shared backing services, one <code class="mn-s42">doze.hcl</code>. No Docker, no compose file, no scripts.</p>
      <div class="mn-s14"><button type="button" class="mn-copy mn-s63" data-copy="git clone https://github.com/doze-dev/doze-examples&#10;cd doze-examples/larder &amp;&amp; doze up" aria-label="Copy the two commands">Copy</button><pre class="mn-term mn-s64"><span class="mn-s9">$</span> git clone https://github.com/doze-dev/doze-examples
<span class="mn-s9">$</span> cd doze-examples/larder &amp;&amp; doze up
<span class="mn-s9"># postgres, redis, kafka, aws, mailpit, then nine services</span></pre></div>
      <div class="mn-stack-sm mn-s65">
        <a class="mn-btn mn-btn-lamp" href="/examples/">Walk through Larder</a>
        <a class="mn-btn mn-btn-ghost" href="https://github.com/doze-dev/doze-examples/blob/main/larder/doze.hcl">Read the doze.hcl on GitHub</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mn-s66">
      <div class="mn-s67"><b class="mn-s68">larder/</b><span class="mn-s69">services by domain</span></div>
      <div class="mn-lang"><div class="mn-lang-h"><span class="mn-lang-dot mn-s70"></span>Go<span class="mn-s71">the core and the gateway</span></div><div class="mn-svc"><span>gateway</span><span>identity</span><span>catalog</span><span>orders</span><span>payments</span></div></div>
      <div class="mn-lang"><div class="mn-lang-h"><span class="mn-lang-dot mn-s72"></span>Python<span class="mn-s71">uv, boto3</span></div><div class="mn-svc"><span>fulfilment</span><span>recommendations</span></div></div>
      <div class="mn-lang"><div class="mn-lang-h"><span class="mn-lang-dot mn-s73"></span>TypeScript<span class="mn-s71">bun, Vite + React</span></div><div class="mn-svc"><span>notifications</span><span>storefront</span></div></div>
      <div class="mn-lang mn-s74"><div class="mn-lang-h"><span class="mn-lang-dot mn-s75"></span>Shared<span class="mn-s71">one each, for every service</span></div><div class="mn-svc"><span>postgres</span><span>redis</span><span>kafka</span><span>aws</span><span>mailpit</span></div></div>
      <span class="mn-s76">Each service owns its own Postgres schema and connects as its own role. Every one gets a name: <code class="mn-s77">gateway.larder.doze</code>, <code class="mn-s77">catalog.larder.doze</code>.</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Popular tools, one line each -->
  <section class="mn-s78">
    <div class="mn-s36">
      <span class="mn-eyebrow">The registry</span>
      <h2 class="mn-h2 mn-s37">Everything your stack uses. One line each.</h2>
      <p class="mn-s62">Postgres with pgvector. Kafka. MongoDB. Mailpit. A whole AWS. No Dockerfiles, no compose YAML, no setup doc: <code class="mn-s42">doze add</code> writes the block, and it sleeps until you need it.</p>
    </div>
    <Popular />
    <a class="mn-s79" href="/registry/">Browse the registry →</a>
  </section>

  <!-- Check it yourself (benchmark with its method; numbers pending) -->
  <section class="mn-s80">
    <div class="mn-s81">
      <span class="mn-eyebrow">Don't take our word for it</span>
      <h2 class="mn-h2">Check it on your own machine.</h2>
      <p class="mn-s62">Every number we publish says the machine, the versions and the date, with the command to run it yourself. Asleep means asleep: go look.</p>
      <pre class="mn-term"><span class="mn-s9">$</span> doze status
  <span class="mn-s9">○</span> postgres  asleep · wakes on a connection
  <span class="mn-s9">○</span> redis     asleep · wakes on a connection
<span class="mn-s9">$</span> pgrep -l postgres
<span class="mn-s9"># nothing. it's asleep.</span></pre>
    </div>
    <figure class="mn-s82">
      <div class="mn-s83"><b class="mn-s84">Memory: Postgres, Valkey and Kafka, after 10 minutes untouched</b><span class="mn-s69">lower is better</span></div>
      <div class="mn-s85">
        <div class="mn-s86"><span class="mn-s87">doze</span><span class="mn-s88"></span><span class="mn-s89">[MB]</span></div>
        <div class="mn-s86"><span class="mn-s90">Docker Desktop</span><span class="mn-s91"></span><span class="mn-s92">[MB]</span></div>
        <div class="mn-s86"><span class="mn-s90">OrbStack</span><span class="mn-s91"></span><span class="mn-s92">[MB]</span></div>
      </div>
      <figcaption class="mn-s93">Bars are drawn equal until measured; none of these numbers exist yet. Method to publish with them: [Mac model, macOS version], [each tool's version], same three engines, median of 5 runs, [date], and the script to reproduce it.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <!-- Everything it does: a long, real checklist -->
  <section class="mn-s44">
    <div class="mn-s45">
      <h2 class="mn-h2 mn-s94">The small things, all done.</h2>
      <div class="mn-s95">
        <div class="mn-chk"><span>✓</span><span>Wakes on the first connection</span></div>
        <div class="mn-chk"><span>✓</span><span>Sleeps after 2 idle minutes, data kept</span></div>
        <div class="mn-chk"><span>✓</span><span>A .doze name for every service</span></div>
        <div class="mn-chk"><span>✓</span><span>Your own domain over https</span></div>
        <div class="mn-chk"><span>✓</span><span>Postgres 14 to 18, built from source</span></div>
        <div class="mn-chk"><span>✓</span><span>pgvector, PostGIS, pg_cron by name <em class="mn-s96">(coming in postgres 0.3)</em></span></div>
        <div class="mn-chk"><span>✓</span><span>doze migrate between Postgres majors</span></div>
        <div class="mn-chk"><span>✓</span><span>doze.lock pins every byte</span></div>
        <div class="mn-chk"><span>✓</span><span>Signed modules, checked on fetch</span></div>
        <div class="mn-chk"><span>✓</span><span>Migrations run once, before the app</span></div>
        <div class="mn-chk"><span>✓</span><span>Connection strings wire themselves</span></div>
        <div class="mn-chk"><span>✓</span><span>Restarts your app when files change</span></div>
        <div class="mn-chk"><span>✓</span><span>Names whoever is holding your port</span></div>
        <div class="mn-chk"><span>✓</span><span>Config mistakes show the line and the fix</span></div>
        <div class="mn-chk"><span>✓</span><span>Spots an app ignoring $PORT</span></div>
        <div class="mn-chk"><span>✓</span><span>Crash loops stop and tell you</span></div>
        <div class="mn-chk"><span>✓</span><span>Logs per run, searchable</span></div>
        <div class="mn-chk"><span>✓</span><span>⌘K: type a verb and a name</span></div>
        <div class="mn-chk"><span>✓</span><span>Menu bar: every stack, one click</span></div>
        <div class="mn-chk"><span>✓</span><span>Quit the app, stacks keep running</span></div>
        <div class="mn-chk"><span>✓</span><span>Per-developer overrides, gitignored</span></div>
        <div class="mn-chk"><span>✓</span><span>doze run for CI, same file</span></div>
        <div class="mn-chk"><span>✓</span><span>One admin prompt, then never again</span></div>
        <div class="mn-chk"><span>✓</span><span>Sends nothing home</span></div>
      </div>
      <a class="mn-s79" href="/changelog/">What changed in each release →</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section class="mn-s97">
    <h2 class="mn-h2 mn-s98">Straight answers</h2>
    <details open><summary>Do I have to give up Docker?</summary><p class="mn-s99">No. Keep containers for building and shipping. doze is for the databases and services you run while you write code.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Is it for production?</summary><p class="mn-s99">No. It is built for your laptop and your CI. That's why it can sleep everything.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What does "asleep" cost me?</summary><p class="mn-s99">The engine's process is stopped and its data stays on disk. One small doze daemon keeps listening and wakes it on the next connection.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Windows?</summary><p class="mn-s99">Not yet. macOS on Apple silicon and Linux today; WSL2 works.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Does it phone home?</summary><p class="mn-s99">No telemetry, no account. It talks to the internet to fetch the engines you declare, and checks their signatures. <a href="/security/">How we handle security</a>.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What does it cost?</summary><p class="mn-s99">Nothing. Apache-2.0, on GitHub.</p></details>
  </section>

  <!-- Closing call -->
  <section class="mn-s100">
    <div class="mn-stack-sm mn-cta mn-s101">
      <div class="mn-stack-sm mn-s102">
        <img class="mn-s103" src="/brand/doze.svg" alt="">
        <div>
          <h2 class="mn-s104">Put your stack to bed.</h2>
          <p class="mn-s105">One file in your repo. One command: doze up.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <a class="mn-btn mn-s106" href="/download/">Download for Mac</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
</Page>

<style>
